{
  "answer": "Wilbur Zelinsky received his master's degree from the University of Wisconsin–Madison. A SAGE encyclopedia entry dates it to 1946. The Wikipedia article names the same school but calls it \"University of Madison, Wisconsin,\" which looks like a slip.\n\nBoth of these sources say his bachelor's (1944) and PhD (1953) were from UC Berkeley. I relied on the search result summaries and did not open the pages.\n\nSources:\n- [Wilbur Zelinsky – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilbur_Zelinsky)\n- [Zelinsky, Wilbur (1921–) – SAGE Encyclopedia](https://sk.sagepub.com/ency/edvol/embed/geography/chpt/zelinsky-wilbur-1921)",
